.TH JACKIT 1 "February 2026" "JackITNG 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jackit \- Terminal-based OSINT and analysis toolkit built with Textual

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jackit
.RI [ options ] " [target]"

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jackit
is a terminal user interface (TUI) application built with Python and
Textual. It provides an interactive environment for managing and executing
analysis tasks, OSINT workflows, and related operational tooling.

The interface is fully keyboard-driven and supports hierarchical screens
with context-aware key bindings.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, --help
Display help information and exit.

.TP
.B \-v, --version
Show version information and exit.

.TP
.B --debug
Enable debug mode.

.TP
.B --config FILE
Specify an alternate configuration file.

.TP
.I target
Optional input target (file, asset, or identifier depending on module).

.SH INTERFACE
The application uses a dynamic key binding system.

Bindings are defined at two levels:

.IP
1. Global bindings defined in the App class.
.br
2. Screen-specific bindings defined per active screen.

When inside a screen, screen-level bindings are displayed after
a delimiter in the footer:

.nf
Q Quit  H Help  |  ESC Close  F1 Info
.fi

Global bindings remain active at all times unless explicitly overridden.

.SH NAVIGATION
The interface is entirely keyboard-driven.

Typical controls:

.TP
.B q
Quit application.

.TP
.B ESC
Close current screen.

.TP
.B F1
Display contextual help.

Additional bindings depend on the active screen.

.SH ARCHITECTURE
.B jackit
uses:

.IP
\- Python 3
.br
\- Textual TUI framework
.br
\- Screen stack navigation model
.br
\- Context-aware binding resolution

Bindings are resolved in the following order:

.IP
Active Screen
.br
Parent Screens
.br
Application (global)

.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration files may be located in:

.nf
~/.jackit/
etc/jackit/
.fi

Exact configuration structure depends on installed modules.

.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.jackit/
User configuration directory.

.TP
.B /usr/share/jackit/
Shared resources.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.

.TP
.B 1
General error.

